  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ opposite to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{3}{BC} \\\\ BC & =\\frac{2}{1}\\cdot 3 \\\\ BC & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
